/* @catalog — generated by `npm run catalog:generate`; do not edit by hand.
 * Internal
 *   Types: Kind, Part
 *   Classes: Storage
 *   Functions: hex, cleanup, db, records, operations, multipart, fileBody, post, send, approve, revision, png,
 *              staged, record, age, later, expectCode, twoColour, chunk, beforeImageData, orientationExif,
 *              apng, deferred, until, reset, early
 *   Constants: guard, actor, other, ordinary, album, artist, track, oldImage, owners, proxy, dependencies,
 *              environment, previous, boundary
 *   Variables: harness, server, base, token, otherToken, userToken, storage, cleaned
 * Tests
 *   - an upload for an Album, an Artist or a MediaTrack is staged privately without changing the catalog
 *   - the staged bytes are normalized: orientation applied and every kind of embedded metadata removed
 *   - refused uploads store no record and send nothing to storage, and an image refusal comes before a filename refusal
 *   - the route checks the item kind, intent key and storage before upload capacity or the body, and needs a declared length and a signed-in administrator
 *   - a client that stops mid-body leaves no record and no staged object, and frees its upload slot
 *   - a replay with the same key and bytes answers the same upload, other bytes conflict, and an unknown transfer is resumed by its retry
 *   - a PUT whose acknowledgement is lost is confirmed by its HEAD, and a HEAD that throws leaves the outcome unknown for the retry
 *   - an upload admitted before its administrator lost the role, or left by a stopped transfer, is staged by its replay or deleted a day after upload
 *   - a live transfer lease is busy, concurrent first requests leave one record, and the upload concurrency guard answers without a code
 *   - a transfer that outlives its lease never overwrites a record the cleanup pass deleted, deletes the object it staged late and answers a conflict
 *   - a transfer that outlives its lease to a retry leaves the record and the object it staged to that retry
 *   - each administrator holds at most sixteen unused uploads, counting unfinished transfers and those whose deletion is not confirmed
 *   - an approval of an upload copies its exact staged object, attaches it under the uploaded name and replays
 *   - an approval refuses another item's, another administrator's, a used, an unknown or a deleting upload, and keeps the existing refusals
 *   - an approval of an upload needs attention, reconciles and cancels exactly as an import source does
 *   - the cleanup pass deletes an unused upload a day after upload, and a used one only once its approval ended
 *   - a failed deletion is recorded, logged once and retried an hour later
 *   - an approval racing a cleanup pass either binds and keeps the upload or finds it deleted
 *   - a late replay of a deleted upload is refused, and an unused upload of a deleted item is still deleted a day later
 *   - a used upload whose item is deleted is kept while its approval needs attention, and deleted once the cancelled approval's cleanup is confirmed
 *   - a worker tick with no operation runs one cleanup pass, and a stopped worker leaves its claim to the lease
 * @end-catalog */

